(3478054, 482720, 52992, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bmartuch:</b></div><hr/><i> Kashi, you did an excellent job on this shot and I think you got robbed. BTW, this is a magnificent portrait shot IMO.  How did you set this up to get the lighting like that and the softness? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This was taken in our living room, at night.<br/> <br/>In front of him (that''s my hubby - bless his heart) is a set of 2 500-watt halogen work-lights on a stand.  They''re to *my* left.<br/> <br/>He''s in front of a piece of white seamless paper that is tacked to the wall.<br/> <br/>HORRIBLE colour cast.  The softness came from what little editing I got to do in Basic.  Levels to change the yellow background to white.  A bit of noise reduction and gaussion blur.  <br/> <br/>Crop, resize, and enter - knew it would be blown away.  But it was fun.</td>', 'Originally posted by bmartuch: Kashi, you did an excellent job on this shot and I think you got robbed. BTW, this is a magnificent portrait shot IMO.  How did you set this up to get the lighting like that and the softness?   This was taken in our living room, at night. In front of him (that''s my hubby - bless his heart) is a set of 2 500-watt halogen work-lights on a stand.  They''re to *my* left. He''s in front of a piece of white seamless paper that is tacked to the wall. HORRIBLE colour cast.  The softness came from what little editing I got to do in Basic.  Levels to change the yellow background to white.  A bit of noise reduction and gaussion blur.   Crop, resize, and enter - knew it would be blown away.  But it was fun.', '2007-03-21 10:37:19.000000', NULL, 0),
